+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+Every tool declares a JSON Schema as its `inputSchema`, and that schema is handed verbatim to the providers, but nothing checks what the model sends back. `ToolRegistry.execute` validates a call's `input` against the resolved definition's `inputSchema` before the executor runs, so a tool that receives unexpected input fails in one predictable way instead of each executor guarding itself differently or not at all.
+
+## The contract of `execute`
+
+- Input missing a `required` property is rejected before the executor runs: `execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property, and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a result naming it, without invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L36)).
+- A property of the wrong declared type is rejected with a message naming the property path and the expected type; neither the returned text nor any log line contains the offending value, because tool input is where identifying data enters the engine ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming its path and expected type, never its value in result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L49)).
+- A static tool's schema is compiled when it is registered, so `register` throws for an uncompilable schema, naming the tool, at startup rather than mid-conversation ([validated by: throws at register time for an uncompilable schema, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L67)).
+- A rejection is a tool result, not an exception: in the orchestrator's tool loop the rejection text reaches the provider on the next round, a corrected retry runs the executor, and `processMessage` resolves ([validated by: feeds the rejection to the provider, runs the corrected retry, and resolves processMessage](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L76)).
+- The tool-round bound is what stops a rejected-and-retried call from spinning.
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared types and `enum` only. It does not inject `additionalProperties: false`, coerce types or apply defaults, so input the schema accepts reaches the executor unmodified, extra properties included.
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` is validated against the schema it returns at that call, not a stale compiled one.
+- `execute` still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` for an unregistered name.
